p18
I1
sVThis privacy policy ("Privacy Policy") applies to users of Posit Science's Apps, and explains how your personal information is collected, used, and disclosed by Posit Science.
p19
I1
sVIf you choose to register for one of our Apps with single-sign-on (SSO) provider, we will collect your name and email address from the SSO provier, and any other information provided or disclosed to you during the SSO registration process.
p20
I1
sVIf you choose to contact us, for example by phone, email, fax, or letter, we collect your contact information as provided in that contact, for example your phone number, email address, fax number, or mailing address, and any information contained in the contact, for example a recording of the phone call, or the contents of the email, fax, or letter.
p21
I1
sVWe may share your Personal Information with the Localization Partner so that they can provide technical support to you.
p22
I1
sVWe do not use Personal Information in such work, nor do we disclose Personal Information in the conduct of such work.
p23
I2
sVSituations Where We Disclose Personal Information About You With Specific Protections for You to Ensure Our Apps Work and You Can Use Them.
p24
I1
sVIn the event of a merger or acquisition transaction or proceeding involving sale, transfer, or divestiture of all or a portion of our business or assets, we may share your Personal Information for the purpose of allowing your continued use of the Apps as managed by the merged or acquiring company.
p25
I1
sVYouTube may share your information with third parties and/or use your information to serve targeted advertising to you on other websites.
p26
I1
sVWe may provide information about the frequency with which you use our Apps (for example, the number of times you used our Apps in a month, or that you did not use our Apps in that month), so that the Insurance Company can evaluate the usage of our Apps by their members and conduct analyses that relate the usage of our Apps to their own records (for example, to determine if people who frequently use our Apps also incur fewer insurance claims).
p27
I1
sVWhen you register for our newsletter, we ask you for and collect your name and email address.
p28
I1
sVIf we become aware that a child under 13 has provided us with personal information, we will take steps to delete such information immediately.
p29
I1
sVIf you choose to add information to your user profile, we will collect that information, such as your mailing address, your date of birth, or your geographical location.
p30
I1
sVIf you become aware that a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us at
p31
I1
sVIn particular, we may provide your Personal Information (for example, your name, your email address, or your insurance policy number) to your Insurance Company, so that your Insurance Company can verify your eligibility for our Apps.
p32
I1
sVWhen you register for one of our Apps, we ask you for and collect your name, email address, and password for your Account.
p33
I1
sVIf you choose to use features of our Apps with other users of our Apps, for example by inviting another user to use BrainHQ, we will share your Personal Information with other users as described by that feature.
p34
I1
sVOur Apps are not directed to individuals under 13 and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
p35
I1
sVWe will not share your other Training Data with the Insurance Company; and specifically, we will not share your cognitive performance data with your Insurance Company.
p36
I2
sVIf your access to our Apps has been provided by a Group, or if at your request we added you to a Group, then your personal information may be shared with that Group so that they can offer their services to you.
p37
I1
sVWe may provide your Personal Information to third party service providers who work on behalf of or with us to provide functionality to our Apps, such as email services and web analytics services.
p38
I1
sVWe store the information about your friend for the purpose of sending this one-time invitation and tracking the success of our referral program.
p39
I1
sVWe may use your mailing address, if provided to us, and other Personal Information to send you informational physical mail (such as a newsletter, or postcards).
p40
I1
sVSpecific Apps may ask you for and collect additional information, such as your date of birth or your insurance policy number.
p41
I1
sVWe do not disclose Personal Information to Distribution Partners.
